+
+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. No key or an unknown key is
+`401 unauthorized`; a known key without permission is `403 forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer`: read only (GET).
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that changes data (any method but GET) is appended to `audit`
+as `{ at, key, method, path, status }` (`key` is the key's name, `null` when
+the key was missing or unknown). `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first
+(managers only).
+
+## Routes added
+
+- `GET /audit`: the audit trail.
